 "text": "The Hyatt Regency Kansas City opened in July 1980. Its centrepiece was a vast atrium, a glass-roofed lobby several storeys high. And crossing it, in mid-air, were three suspended walkways. The second-floor walkway hung directly beneath the one on the fourth floor. The third-floor walkway ran on its own, off to one side.",
